The Smart Recovery driver provides a custom Fuse layer implementation that uses
metadata descriptors to combine raw volume files with sparse physical disk
images, remapped to provide a virtual disk image matching the original
protected system physical volume structure. This implementation is able to
perform both basic volume mapping as well as dynamically recreate complex
volume structures, like rebuilding a software RAID5 Windows Dynamic disk set
from the single volume file stored by the Replibit backend.
Smart Recovery is a new feature being implemented for Appliances, Legacy Vaults
and Infinity Cloud to improve the recovery experience of our Partners. By
implementing this feature, recovery operations will now be able to return
virtual disks structured identically to the original Protected System disk
layout, making it much easier to recover to physical systems and resolving many
challenges we currently have with booting and recovering systems with
non-standard or complex partition configurations. This driver provides the
foundation layer necessary to support Smart Recovery for both Infinity Cloud
and AxCloud Virtual Office.

